#only("1")[#voiceover("That's not quite right. Let's look at the correct solution.")]
// Very briefly talk about why a) is incorrect
#only("2")[#voiceover("Option a) Ignoring past investments is incorrect. In fact, the sunk cost fallacy is the opposite - it's when you consider past investments too much in your decision making.")]
// Very briefly talk about why b) is correct
#only("3")[#voiceover("Option b) Continuing an endeavor due to past investments is the correct definition of the sunk cost fallacy. It's when you continue something just because you've already invested time, money, or effort into it.")]
// Very briefly talk about why c) is incorrect
#only("4")[#voiceover("Option c) Making decisions based on future benefits is incorrect. While considering future benefits is generally a good thing in decision making, it's not what the sunk cost fallacy is about.")]
