]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Sunk Cost Fallacy Explained]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[🧮 Sunk costs = Past, unrecoverable costs]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[🤔 Fallacy: Basing decisions on sunk costs]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[❌ Leads to continuing unprofitable endeavors]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[✅ Rational decision: Based on future costs & benefits]

#only("1")[#voiceover("Sunk costs are costs that have already been incurred and cannot be recovered. They are in the past.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("The sunk cost fallacy is the mistake of basing current decisions on these past, irrecoverable costs.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("This often leads to continuing endeavors or investments that are no longer profitable, just because you've already put resources into them.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("However, rational decision making should be based on future costs and benefits, not on past costs that can't be changed.")]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example of Sunk Cost Fallacy]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[🎥 You paid \$10 for a movie ticket]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[😴 30 minutes in, you realize the movie is boring]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[🤔 You think, "I paid for this, I should stay till the end"]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[❌ That's the sunk cost fallacy in action!]
#v(20pt)
#only("5-")[✅ Rational decision: Leave if you won't enjoy the rest]

#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's look at an example. Imagine you paid 10 dollars for a movie ticket.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("30 minutes into the movie, you realize it's really boring and you're not enjoying it at all.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("You might think, 'Well, I paid for this ticket, I should stay until the end to get my money's worth.'")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("That's the sunk cost fallacy in action! You're basing your decision on the past cost of the ticket, which you can't get back regardless of whether you stay or leave.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("The rational decision would be to leave if you don't think you'll enjoy the rest of the movie. The ticket price is a sunk cost and shouldn't factor into your decision.")]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Avoiding the Sunk Cost Fallacy]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[🧠 Be aware of the fallacy]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[🔍 Identify sunk costs in your decisions]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[🔮 Base decisions on future, not past]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[💰 Don't throw good money after bad]
#v(20pt)
#only("5-")[🎯 Focus on your goals, not past investments]

#only("1")[#voiceover("To avoid falling for the sunk cost fallacy, the first step is to be aware of it.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("When making a decision, try to identify any sunk costs that might be influencing you.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("Remember to base your decisions on future costs and benefits, not on past investments that can't be recovered.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("Don't keep investing in something just because you've already put resources into it. That's just throwing good money after bad.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("Always keep your goals in mind. If continuing an endeavor won't help you reach your goals, it's best to cut your losses and move on, regardless of what you've already invested.")]
]